# Contact form → your inbox, via EmailJS (no backend needed).
# 1. Create a free account at https://www.emailjs.com
# 2. Add an Email Service (connect your Gmail) -> copy the Service ID
# 3. Create an Email Template with variables: from_name, from_email,
#    subject, message, to_email -> copy the Template ID
# 4. Account -> General -> copy your Public Key
# Paste all three below (or set them in Vercel Project Settings ->
# Environment Variables). Without these, the form falls back to opening
# a pre-filled mailto: link, so the site still works with zero setup.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
